builtin_trees -- embedded Unity engine-class type-tree database
Location in this distribution: src/builtin_trees/2022.3.62f2.bin
  (embedded into the built library and CLI by src/builtin_trees.zig, so it
  travels in binary releases as well as in the source package)

The file is a repack of the Unity 2022.3.62f2 StructsDump published by the
AssetRipper TypeTreeDumps project
(https://github.com/AssetRipper/TypeTreeDumps), produced by
scripts/structsdump-to-builtin.py, whose header records the exact source
path and the command used. No AssetRipper source code is vendored here --
only the dumped layout table, re-encoded into this project's own binary
format.

The shipped bytes are pinned by digest, because the dump is fetched from a
moving upstream branch and carries no checksum of its own:

  src/builtin_trees/2022.3.62f2.bin
    sha256  6e1a6f760832a3740f9637275845e6102d8a0de36a536f12f0508fb6f743c4c2
    size    425875 bytes

A test in src/builtin_trees.zig recomputes that digest, so the shipped table
can be traced to a known repack and refreshing a release means updating both
the file and the line above deliberately.

The content is Unity's own engine-class field layout metadata (per node:
type name, field name, nesting level, version, byte size and serializer
flags) as emitted by Unity's serializer. It carries no Unity code, no
AssetRipper code, and no game content.

The dump's own distribution terms are not recorded in this tree. Anyone
redistributing the shipped .bin should confirm them at the origin above.
